2. Standard User Login Flow (e.g., Admin)
This diagram shows how any registered user logs in to receive a JWT, which is required for subsequent authenticated actions.

@startuml
title 2. Standard User Login Flow (e.g., Admin)

actor "Client" as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "User Service\n(Spring Boot)" as Service
database "Database" as DB

skinparam sequenceActorStyle awesome

== Login Request ==

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/auth/login\nBody: {email, password}
Gateway -> Service: Forward Request
activate Service

Service -> DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?
activate DB
DB --> Service: Return User record (with hashed password & role)
deactivate DB

alt Credentials are Valid
    note right of Service
        Spring Security's AuthenticationManager
        compares the plaintext password from the
        request with the hashed password from the DB.
    end note
    Service -> Service: **Generate Signed JWT**\n(with userId, email, role, expiration)
    Service --> Gateway: **200 OK**\nBody: { "jwt": "..." }
else Credentials are Invalid
    Service --> Gateway: **401 Unauthorized**
end

Gateway --> Client: Return response (200 or 401)
deactivate Service

Client -> Client: Securely store JWT for future requests

@enduml